From 199781679240978888c57558687c024a50acb0f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 12:00:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] Round 7: Add a sixteen-lane AVX-512 lane kernel

Make the lockstep lane kernel generic over its width. On hosts with
AVX-512F, preparation selects a sixteen-lane build compiled with the
avx512f target feature, which keeps two eight-lane dependency chains in
32 vector registers; other hosts keep eight lanes with AVX2 or the
baseline build. The engine groups rows and distributes worker ranges in
units of the selected width. Rust does not contract multiplies and adds,
so lanes perform the same IEEE operations and records stay
byte-identical. A unit test compares the AVX-512, AVX2 and baseline
kernels bit for bit; the lockstep test covers up to 18 rows per model.

An earlier round 7 attempt (validated fast decoding of parameter
arrays) measured 0.955x on the invalid workload and was reverted; its
timing is in evidence/performance-0.3.0/rejected/.

Workload: domain (48 full records, PD control, 4,000 RK4 steps each,
one worker).
Before median: 1.038 ms. After median: 0.705 ms. Speedup: 1.47x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
